{title: Deck the Halls}

{columns: 2}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 1"}

[D]Deck the halls with boughs of holly
[G]Fa-la-la-la-[D]laah, la-[A7]la-la-[D]la
[D]'Tis the season to be jolly
[G]Fa-la-la-la-[D]laah, la-[A7]la-la-[D]la
[A7]Don we now our [D]gay apparel
[D]Fa-la-la, [G]la-la-la, [A7]la-la-la
[D]Toll the ancient Yule-tide carol
[G]Fa-la-la-la-[D]laah, la-[A7]la-la-[D]la

{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 2"}

[D]See the blazing Yule before us
[G]Fa-la-la-la-[D]laah, la-[A7]la-la-[D]la
[D]Strike the harp and join the chorus
[G]Fa-la-la-la-[D]laah, la-[A7]la-la-[D]la
[A7]Follow me in [D]merry measure
[D]Fa-la-la, [G]la-la-la, [A7]la-la-la
[D]While I tell of Yule-tide treasure
[G]Fa-la-la-la-[D]laah, la-[A7]la-la-[D]la

{end_of_verse}

{column_break}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 3"}

[D]Fast away the old year passes
[G]Fa-la-la-la-[D]laah, la-[A7]la-la-[D]la
[D]Hail the new year, lads and lasses
[G]Fa-la-la-la-[D]laah, la-[A7]la-la-[D]la
[A7]Sing we joyous, [D]all together
[D]Fa-la-la, [G]la-la-la, [A7]la-la-la
[D]Heedless of the wind and weather
[G]Fa-la-la-la-[D]laah, la-[A7]la-la-[D]la

{end_of_verse}

{comment: Slowly}

[G]Fa-la-la-la-[D]laah, la-[A7]la-la-[D]la